===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# The process of [[buy]]ing [[goods]] or [[service]]s, or searching for those suitable to buy.
#: {{ux|en|On Saturdays we usually do the '''shopping'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Landon Ethel Churchill|page=280|volume=I|passage=After a hard day's '''shopping''', they had come home laden with bargains, and the dressing-room was strewed with Indian fans, ivory boxes, and lace.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1887|author=Harriet W. Daly|title=Digging, Squatting, and Pioneering Life in the Northern Territory of South Australia|page=132|passage=Here I began my '''shopping''', was interviewed by dressmakers, and naturally had much to do to habit myself for civilized life again.}}
#* {{RQ:Travers Cuckoo in the Nest|chapter=2|passage=Mother{{...}}considered that the exclusiveness of Peter's circle was due not to its distinction, but to the fact that it was an inner Babylon of prodigality and whoredom, from which every Kensingtonian held aloof, except on the conventional tip-and-run excursions in pursuit of '''shopping''', tea and theatres.}}
# Recently bought goods.
#: {{ux|en|I carried three heavy bags of '''shopping''' up the stairs.}}
# An area's combination of [[store]]s and other infrastructure and products available for people who want to shop.
#: {{ux|en|Boston has good '''shopping'''.}}
# Placement in a [[workshop]] for [[overhaul]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1961|month=November|title=Talking of Trains: The roller-bearing A1s|journal=Trains Illustrated|page=643|text=The five roller-bearing A1s are now averaging 120,000 miles between '''shopping'''; this figure is an improvement of about 50 per cent on the norm of other ex-L.N.E. Pacific types.}}

====Usage notes====
* In English, ''do the shopping'' and ''go shopping'' are commonly used expressions. See [[Appendix:Collocations of do, have, make, and take]]

